# Keep bytes EXACTLY as committed: `-text` tells git never to convert or renormalize,
# whatever core.autocrlf says. That preserves endings; it does not keep CRLF out.
# Tracked text outside dist/ and .pynifly/ is LF-only, and the pre-commit hook and the
# test suite enforce it (scripts/repo_hygiene.py, #lf-only). dist/ and .pynifly/ keep
# the endings their upstream bytes carry.
* -text

# Tracked binaries: also never diff as text.
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.pyd  binary
*.zip  binary
*.nif  binary
*.tri  binary
*.osd  binary
*.dds  binary
*.bsa  binary
